WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:35.618 --> 00:38.788
TWO YEARS AGO

00:56.806 --> 00:57.640
Cellar spiders.

01:03.271 --> 01:05.231
They turn houses into abandoned houses.

01:06.816 --> 01:08.151
You should kill them on sight.

01:24.709 --> 01:26.503
But this isn't a house.

01:39.140 --> 01:41.226
Please sign on the line marked "NM."

01:41.726 --> 01:44.187
We also offer a special shipping service
for this product--

01:44.270 --> 01:45.522
I'll just take it myself.

01:46.064 --> 01:46.898
I'll be taking a cab.

02:04.207 --> 02:08.044
You can see that the compartments
are very convenient.

02:08.837 --> 02:11.297
It'll be helpful
when organizing your baby's things.

02:13.216 --> 02:15.009
Could we also take a look

02:16.177 --> 02:18.263
at the trunk that woman just left with?

02:18.346 --> 02:19.180
Yes, of course.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.226
I'm going to step out.

02:24.519 --> 02:25.353
Sure.

02:52.463 --> 02:53.840
Divorce him, Ms. Noh In-ji.

03:01.598 --> 03:02.891
Your father's passed.

03:04.434 --> 03:06.436
I'm saying this is
where your punishment ends.

03:08.897 --> 03:10.857
Both sides will receive alimony.

03:12.233 --> 03:14.319
It's our fault the contract fell apart.

03:16.404 --> 03:17.238
I also

03:18.364 --> 03:19.866
got married through NM.

03:23.995 --> 03:25.079
I'm sure you knew that.

04:53.960 --> 04:55.169
Why aren't you sleeping?

04:57.547 --> 04:59.966
Is what Ms. Lee Seo-yeon said
keeping you up?

05:09.058 --> 05:12.145
Did you know you kick the sheets
in your sleep?

05:13.479 --> 05:15.356
Are you staying awake to tuck me in?

05:16.357 --> 05:18.234
At least one of us should be at ease.

05:43.718 --> 05:45.970
What would make you feel at ease?

05:48.681 --> 05:51.225
It would be even better
if both of us are at ease.

05:53.686 --> 05:55.521
We wake up tomorrow morning

05:56.898 --> 05:59.275
to find that we've aged about 20 years.

06:05.323 --> 06:07.450
We find each other predictable and boring.

06:08.659 --> 06:10.912
I know all the people that you know,

06:11.662 --> 06:13.956
and you know all the people that I know.

06:16.667 --> 06:19.796
Gossiping about them one by one
gives us joy.

06:20.713 --> 06:23.549
With sleep still in our eyes,
we have breakfast together.

06:25.676 --> 06:28.805
We're stuck together the whole day,
bored by each other's company.

06:32.683 --> 06:34.060
We grumble and complain,

06:34.936 --> 06:36.687
then grill some fish for dinner

06:37.855 --> 06:39.273
and doze off together.

06:41.609 --> 06:43.945
The next day,
we wake up like the day before.

06:45.113 --> 06:46.531
Sounds incredibly dull.

06:49.534 --> 06:50.368
Maybe.

06:51.411 --> 06:54.080
I'll be that predictable person for you.

08:04.817 --> 08:06.736
He's suddenly disappeared.

08:07.278 --> 08:09.197
I'd been tracking him
through a chain of brokers.

08:12.450 --> 08:13.868
I'll stop if you tell me to.

08:15.369 --> 08:16.204
No.

08:17.663 --> 08:18.831
Please keep searching.

08:25.004 --> 08:26.172
Five months?

08:27.548 --> 08:28.508
Twenty-four weeks.

08:29.800 --> 08:31.677
Your husband hasn't changed his mind?

08:32.345 --> 08:34.514
What are they gonna do?
I can't have the procedure now.

08:47.151 --> 08:49.654
SENDER NOH IN-JI
DEPOSIT 20,000,000 WON

08:52.031 --> 08:52.949
It's too much.

08:53.032 --> 08:55.409
You'll have a lot to do
once the baby arrives.

08:56.035 --> 08:57.912
Get a room first, even if it's small.

08:59.413 --> 09:01.290
Somewhere your husband won't find.

09:08.130 --> 09:11.133
I never thought I'd find myself thanking

09:12.343 --> 09:13.678
a rude-ass southerner.

09:15.680 --> 09:16.847
If you lose your child,

09:17.390 --> 09:19.183
you'll look back on this time
as a living hell.

09:19.809 --> 09:21.227
No need to thank me in advance.

09:23.062 --> 09:25.189
Don't get too attached to marriage either.

09:26.232 --> 09:27.066
Divorce is…

09:34.615 --> 09:35.825
no big deal.

09:47.753 --> 09:49.505
You have to see this.

10:26.208 --> 10:27.960
HAN JEONG-WON

10:31.380 --> 10:32.548
When did you leave?

10:33.466 --> 10:34.550
Early this morning.

10:35.968 --> 10:37.219
Why? Is something wrong?

10:38.054 --> 10:40.014
No, I was just wondering
if something was up.

10:42.350 --> 10:43.517
Good to know you're okay.

10:44.185 --> 10:45.061
All right.

10:45.144 --> 10:47.605
I'm afraid I can't join you
for breakfast today.

11:26.769 --> 11:31.482
Ms. Do-dam said someone's been sneaking in
and killing the goldfish every night.

11:31.565 --> 11:34.819
I thought it was just nonsense,
but she made me uneasy.

11:34.902 --> 11:36.404
So I recorded some footage,

11:37.113 --> 11:38.781
but I never expected to see this.

11:41.283 --> 11:43.828
That's the homeowner prick, right?
The attempted spouse.

11:45.287 --> 11:48.416
So what should I call him? Aquaman?

11:50.376 --> 11:51.544
It wasn't him.

11:53.254 --> 11:55.005
I'd know if he had been here.

11:55.548 --> 11:59.343
Who else would come through the front door
in the middle of the night

11:59.427 --> 12:01.887
just to stare into the fish tank
like some nutjob?

13:00.404 --> 13:03.324
Buy me some food, would you?
I want to talk.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.767
I feel weird whenever I eat this.

13:31.393 --> 13:35.105
It reminds me that the things we eat
were all alive and kicking once.

13:36.524 --> 13:39.652
It's only natural to feel uneasy
when eating another's flesh.

13:46.408 --> 13:47.535
That's what makes it good.

13:50.079 --> 13:51.163
If this is why you--

13:51.247 --> 13:53.999
Of course,
we're here to discuss Noh In-ji.

14:04.009 --> 14:06.929
You know about the perverted sicko
she almost married, don't you?

14:10.099 --> 14:11.809
So you do know.

14:13.352 --> 14:14.812
She's registered at his address.

14:14.895 --> 14:18.649
My point is, it's been five years
since that fucker disappeared,

14:18.732 --> 14:20.526
but she's still there.

14:22.653 --> 14:24.822
Why is she so hung up
on that dirty bastard anyway?

14:26.115 --> 14:26.949
Don't you agree?

14:29.118 --> 14:32.079
Call the cops. Whether or not it was him,
we have a problem.

14:32.872 --> 14:34.832
And say what? This isn't even my house.

14:35.541 --> 14:37.960
"Someone broke into
the apartment of my ex-fiancé,

14:38.043 --> 14:40.296
who disappeared five years ago,
to clean the fish tank"?

14:40.796 --> 14:42.339
Should I also mention

14:42.423 --> 14:44.717
that I'm still living in his house
just to spite him?

14:44.800 --> 14:46.552
Is that what I should tell the cops?

14:46.635 --> 14:47.803
Damn it.

14:49.138 --> 14:50.014
For starters,

14:51.015 --> 14:52.182
I'll change the door code.

14:53.893 --> 14:56.228
Don't tell Ms. Do-dam the new code.

14:56.312 --> 14:57.730
She's a total blabbermouth.

14:59.899 --> 15:00.733
In-ji.

15:01.901 --> 15:03.903
You do know this isn't normal, right?

15:08.073 --> 15:09.325
Where are you going?

15:09.408 --> 15:10.993
I need to check something.

15:15.331 --> 15:19.126
She was in our workshop
for about three months.

15:19.209 --> 15:22.379
Her company offered perks
for soon-to-be-married star employees,

15:22.463 --> 15:23.380
like cooking classes.

15:24.715 --> 15:27.301
I thought they looked great together
until I found out.

15:27.384 --> 15:30.179
Like those picture-perfect couples
that make you do a double take.

15:31.347 --> 15:32.222
But in the end,

15:32.306 --> 15:36.477
I had to witness Noh In-ji's life
fall apart right before my eyes.

15:38.604 --> 15:39.438
"Fall apart"?

15:39.939 --> 15:43.859
A week or so before the wedding,
a string of photos surfaced online.

15:44.818 --> 15:47.321
Photos of men
climbing all over each other…

15:50.115 --> 15:51.200
nibbling and sucking.

15:54.036 --> 15:56.872
What do you think happened
after thousands of people saw them?

16:05.506 --> 16:06.966
The guy vanished,

16:08.425 --> 16:10.177
leaving In-ji to deal with the fallout.

16:10.970 --> 16:12.930
Those fucking conglomerate bastards.

16:13.597 --> 16:15.516
Their legal team asked her for a statement

16:15.599 --> 16:17.810
and promised
it wouldn't come up again later.

16:19.019 --> 16:21.146
They didn't want
to be labeled homo-haters.

16:25.776 --> 16:27.778
I bet you don't even know what hate is.

16:30.948 --> 16:32.116
You have no idea…

16:34.201 --> 16:38.372
how hatred can make
a person shrivel inside.

16:46.714 --> 16:49.091
Noh In-ji is an orphan.

16:49.925 --> 16:52.845
She cut ties with her family
and disconnected from her emotions.

16:55.556 --> 16:58.726
She's so fucking tenacious.

17:01.228 --> 17:03.647
That's why I worship her.

17:14.992 --> 17:16.452
Why not just call me a bitch?

17:16.535 --> 17:19.288
You people think vulgarity
levels the playing field.

17:19.371 --> 17:21.081
Why aren't you saying anything?

17:22.124 --> 17:23.083
Because I know.

17:25.544 --> 17:27.421
Do you really want a divorce?

17:29.465 --> 17:30.299
Yeah.

17:30.799 --> 17:33.552
You'll be miserable
with Mr. Han Jeong-won.

17:34.887 --> 17:36.472
You'd be happy with me.

17:38.599 --> 17:39.767
You're just delusional.

17:40.434 --> 17:41.643
Or maybe it's your work ethic.

17:47.733 --> 17:49.693
- Double-check, just in case.
- Of course.

17:50.694 --> 17:52.237
The employees are hardworking.

17:52.321 --> 17:54.490
I'm sure we'll finish on time.

18:13.175 --> 18:14.510
This room is the last one.

18:15.219 --> 18:17.679
Let me know what you'd like,
and I'll be happy to accommodate.

18:18.931 --> 18:20.516
What on earth are you thinking?

18:21.100 --> 18:22.184
You mean the divorce?

18:23.894 --> 18:27.272
You're the one who said
I should go ahead with this marriage.

18:27.898 --> 18:29.608
This is no longer just between us.

18:30.359 --> 18:31.777
So it's between the four of us?

18:33.654 --> 18:35.781
When you violate a contract,
you pay the fine.

18:35.864 --> 18:37.616
There's no more or less to it.

18:45.165 --> 18:47.668
Stop resisting
and just take the meds I gave you.

18:47.751 --> 18:50.337
Are drugs your solution to everything?

18:50.838 --> 18:52.923
Why the hell did you change your mind?

18:55.300 --> 18:57.136
Because I've seen all I needed to.

18:58.053 --> 18:59.513
Do I need to explain further?

19:00.597 --> 19:02.266
End things quickly with Noh In-ji.

19:03.350 --> 19:05.144
So we can return to normal
just as quickly.

19:24.121 --> 19:26.039
OPEN DOOR

19:27.708 --> 19:30.002
Are drugs your solution to everything?

19:31.420 --> 19:33.338
Why the hell did you change your mind?

19:39.970 --> 19:43.056
Come get me.
I'm not feeling well and need to go home.

19:44.099 --> 19:45.601
I don't think I can right now.

19:46.393 --> 19:47.436
We have a guest.

19:48.645 --> 19:49.479
"A guest"?

19:50.105 --> 19:52.399
Ms. Noh In-ji is here.

20:14.755 --> 20:16.423
Tea is boring. Try this.

20:17.049 --> 20:18.800
It's non-alcoholic, but it's not bad.

20:22.804 --> 20:24.264
I didn't think you'd come here.

20:27.726 --> 20:29.269
I needed to check something.

20:30.562 --> 20:32.272
And what will you do after checking?

20:34.274 --> 20:35.901
Do you know the Judgment of Solomon?

20:35.984 --> 20:38.153
The story of the real mother
and the fake mother?

20:40.072 --> 20:41.073
SEO-YEON

20:43.951 --> 20:45.035
Sir!

20:46.203 --> 20:47.788
Would you please step on it?

20:49.665 --> 20:51.917
That judgment always struck me as odd.

20:52.584 --> 20:56.088
Fake mom or not, how could anyone agree
to a baby being cut in half?

20:56.755 --> 20:59.007
Her callous disregard for the baby's life

21:00.133 --> 21:01.843
implies she was but an empty husk,

21:01.927 --> 21:04.263
alive but not truly living.

21:06.265 --> 21:07.349
I feel sorry for her.

21:08.600 --> 21:11.270
Or maybe she was the biggest bitch

21:12.020 --> 21:14.147
of 3,000 years ago.

21:19.528 --> 21:21.029
She'll be here soon.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.665
You shouldn't let wine stains sit.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.209
Use the upstairs bathroom.

21:35.585 --> 21:37.546
It's just to the left…

21:39.548 --> 21:40.716
of Seo-yeon's study.

23:30.992 --> 23:33.203
No, I was just wondering
if something was up.

23:34.162 --> 23:35.330
Good to know you're okay.

23:36.248 --> 23:37.082
All right.

23:38.083 --> 23:40.377
I'm afraid I can't join you
for breakfast today.

24:04.443 --> 24:05.569
When will you be home?

24:36.516 --> 24:37.684
Why didn't you pick up?

24:39.519 --> 24:40.896
I forgot to bring my phone.

24:41.688 --> 24:42.606
I was in the bath.

24:44.774 --> 24:45.901
Where's Ms. Noh In-ji?

24:46.443 --> 24:47.527
She left a while ago.

24:48.737 --> 24:50.363
I should have told you she left.

24:57.913 --> 24:59.122
What did you talk about?

24:59.706 --> 25:03.210
A strategy meeting between colleagues
ahead of a contract cancellation.

25:05.462 --> 25:08.590
Would telling you that
give you peace of mind?

26:01.101 --> 26:02.060
What did you do today?

26:03.895 --> 26:06.773
I met a friend because something happened
at my old house.

26:09.192 --> 26:10.026
Your old house…

26:14.281 --> 26:15.991
I ran into someone I know.

26:16.866 --> 26:19.035
We're not close,
but we ended up drinking soju together.

26:21.204 --> 26:22.664
Did you enjoy the soju?

26:25.542 --> 26:26.459
I don't remember.

26:45.729 --> 26:47.897
Why don't you head upstairs with the beer?

26:49.733 --> 26:50.567
Sure.

27:53.129 --> 27:54.089
I found her supplier.

27:55.090 --> 27:57.342
Mr. Yoon.
Seems like he's famous on the scene.

27:59.010 --> 28:00.470
Where can I find him?

28:11.856 --> 28:13.274
Got more of that stuff?

28:15.819 --> 28:16.945
Let's talk in person.

28:21.991 --> 28:23.576
I'll come to your office tomorrow.

29:10.623 --> 29:13.168
Did you use Jeong-won's phone
to mess with me?

29:14.461 --> 29:17.589
I just wanted to know
why you're doing this.

29:18.757 --> 29:19.924
Do you know Han Jeong-won?

29:20.425 --> 29:22.343
I'm guessing you think you do.

29:23.178 --> 29:24.637
Is that why you do this?

29:25.722 --> 29:26.973
You're crossing the line.

29:28.266 --> 29:29.768
You two will be divorced soon anyway.

29:31.227 --> 29:32.061
No.

29:32.812 --> 29:34.230
We won't be getting a divorce

29:34.939 --> 29:36.107
because I refuse.

29:38.026 --> 29:41.196
The manual states only the married couple
can decide to divorce.

29:42.155 --> 29:43.656
Isn't that how marriages work?

29:46.785 --> 29:48.703
Leave him alone.

29:50.121 --> 29:51.331
I came here to warn you.

29:54.959 --> 29:57.962
You should've said that sooner,
and to your mother.

29:59.464 --> 30:01.341
You should've said,
"Don't mess with my man."

30:03.218 --> 30:07.889
Come to think of it, you have a knack
for making those around you miserable,

30:09.307 --> 30:10.475
even though you're a nobody.

30:12.769 --> 30:14.354
I finally know for sure

30:15.355 --> 30:17.232
that, even 3,000 years later,

30:18.316 --> 30:20.443
bitches will be bitches.

30:54.310 --> 30:57.981
These pills are like meth.
Why do you keep pushing them on him?

31:01.234 --> 31:03.444
Do you really think
I gave him those to take?

31:04.153 --> 31:05.071
Why else?

31:06.739 --> 31:09.325
I don't think I owe you an explanation.

31:15.123 --> 31:16.291
Does your client know?

31:17.584 --> 31:20.962
That you hired a junkie to work on-site
just to get your hands on this stuff?

31:23.172 --> 31:27.051
Was that enough of a threat
to give you nightmares tonight?

31:28.469 --> 31:30.221
Or do I need to move to plan B?

31:43.234 --> 31:44.402
Are you threatening me?

31:46.988 --> 31:48.489
It's more than just a threat.

31:49.073 --> 31:50.325
What kind of person

31:50.825 --> 31:53.912
installs a camera in the same spot
Han Jeong-won's despicable father used

31:53.995 --> 31:55.663
to spy on his mother?

32:04.631 --> 32:06.299
You'd hoped he'd give in and take these!

32:08.134 --> 32:10.887
You needed to break Han Jeong-won
so he'd come back to you!

32:12.138 --> 32:14.432
Did you get a kick out of spying on him
through the cameras?

32:15.266 --> 32:18.853
Did you feel like a god
having him in the palm of your hand?

32:20.355 --> 32:21.981
How could anyone do such things?

32:22.649 --> 32:24.901
And you still call yourself human?

32:35.536 --> 32:36.955
Why are you doing all this?

32:37.455 --> 32:39.165
Why are you taking this so far?

33:09.362 --> 33:10.530
What the hell would you know?

33:11.030 --> 33:12.490
This is between me and Jeong-won!

33:12.991 --> 33:14.617
This is our life!

33:14.701 --> 33:16.119
Whose life?

34:03.082 --> 34:04.751
Aren't we getting divorced?

34:04.834 --> 34:07.003
How can I get over you
if you act like this?

34:09.756 --> 34:11.340
I can never say no to you,

34:11.966 --> 34:13.426
so there's no way for me to stop it.

34:14.719 --> 34:16.054
I'm only human.

34:35.948 --> 34:37.325
The director likes the music.

34:37.825 --> 34:40.078
They did ask for small changes
here and there.

34:41.871 --> 34:44.832
I guess they share your eccentric taste.

34:46.334 --> 34:49.087
What happens with Ms. Noh In-ji
once your contract ends?

34:53.257 --> 34:55.301
I hope you won't go back to Seo-yeon.

34:56.385 --> 34:58.513
I don't know what Lee Seo-yeon's thinking,

34:58.596 --> 35:00.848
but for you,
it's an opportunity to escape.

35:00.932 --> 35:01.766
Don't you agree?

35:02.600 --> 35:04.310
Seo-yeon told me to get a divorce.

35:04.811 --> 35:05.937
That crazy…

35:08.856 --> 35:10.066
I've fallen for Noh In-ji.

35:14.904 --> 35:15.863
Since when?

35:16.906 --> 35:18.407
It's a long story.

35:21.577 --> 35:25.540
You know you can't have
a serious relationship with her, right?

35:28.584 --> 35:29.710
Why not?

35:30.294 --> 35:31.337
Didn't you read the manual?

35:32.797 --> 35:35.049
You literally can't do anything
with Noh In-ji.

35:35.133 --> 35:37.760
"Couples matched through NM
may only be married through NM."

35:37.844 --> 35:40.221
It's the very first thing
written in the manual.

35:50.064 --> 35:52.692
Fucking hell, how do you do it again?

35:52.775 --> 35:53.609
Maybe like this?

35:55.736 --> 35:56.654
Right.

36:04.328 --> 36:05.371
The hell are you doing?

36:21.012 --> 36:22.346
She says it's not that punk.

36:24.015 --> 36:25.641
Do you agree that it's not him?

36:26.392 --> 36:27.768
My vision is all blurry.

36:27.852 --> 36:28.936
I can't tell.

36:30.146 --> 36:31.397
My eyes are going.

36:32.064 --> 36:34.859
Your eyes have been going
for a good while now.

36:35.526 --> 36:37.570
Just take a closer look.

36:39.614 --> 36:42.033
- Five years is a long time.
- It really is.

36:43.034 --> 36:45.953
If he'd said something before leaving,
In-ji wouldn't keep coming back here.

36:46.537 --> 36:49.123
She wouldn't care
what happened to this house.

36:49.957 --> 36:51.542
I honestly think

36:51.626 --> 36:54.545
she's been acting this way
because he never gave her closure.

38:22.216 --> 38:23.634
Have you eaten?

38:26.220 --> 38:27.179
No.

38:29.265 --> 38:30.516
I'm hungry.

38:38.399 --> 38:42.069
Two cheeseburger combos
without tomatoes, please.

38:42.153 --> 38:43.195
Sure.

38:44.071 --> 38:45.823
I'll have that ready for you
in just a sec.

38:55.791 --> 38:58.878
Your cheeseburgers are ready.
Please enjoy.

38:59.420 --> 39:00.254
Thank you.

39:18.606 --> 39:20.649
I asked for them to be removed
from both burgers

39:21.609 --> 39:22.818
because we're vegetarians.

39:26.238 --> 39:27.073
Thank you.

39:33.329 --> 39:34.872
I missed you all day.

39:39.585 --> 39:41.754
Missing you has made it a tough day.

39:54.433 --> 39:56.268
It wasn't as bad for me.

40:16.414 --> 40:17.790
I missed you too.

42:13.489 --> 42:14.698
Back up.

42:15.616 --> 42:18.327
I'll back us out of here.

42:18.410 --> 42:19.578
I'm good now, aren't I?

42:24.083 --> 42:25.960
Why'd you learn to kayak?

42:26.043 --> 42:27.169
Because I couldn't swim.

42:28.587 --> 42:29.421
Seriously?

42:30.673 --> 42:33.551
I almost drowned in a river
when I was little.

42:35.803 --> 42:37.972
After that,
I couldn't bring myself to swim.

42:40.182 --> 42:42.393
I tried to learn again
when I was in college…

42:44.436 --> 42:45.271
but then,

42:47.147 --> 42:49.316
a close friend of mine drowned.

42:50.401 --> 42:51.527
It was suicide.

42:55.614 --> 42:56.949
I haven't been able to swim since.

43:01.412 --> 43:04.873
I only meant to ask
why you learned how to kayak.

43:05.958 --> 43:07.918
Now I'm hesitant to ask you anything else.

43:12.506 --> 43:14.049
Why do you enjoy kayaking?

43:19.096 --> 43:21.181
When I'm on a kayak,
I feel like an island.

43:23.058 --> 43:26.979
Like I'm a floating island
that no one can reach.

43:57.551 --> 43:59.386
HUSBAND

44:02.640 --> 44:03.474
Yes?

44:05.601 --> 44:06.852
I'll head out right away.

44:23.786 --> 44:26.830
Ms. Lee, I gave you a job.
Shouldn't there be some progress by now?

44:26.914 --> 44:28.165
What's the status?

44:30.250 --> 44:33.379
You kept me in the dark so long,
I just had to come to see you.

44:35.214 --> 44:36.256
Who…

44:50.229 --> 44:51.105
What tea is this?

44:52.231 --> 44:53.232
It tastes great.

44:57.277 --> 44:59.196
Could you pack some for me before I leave?

45:03.617 --> 45:04.743
Why are you here?

45:07.579 --> 45:10.708
It's such a small world,

45:11.417 --> 45:12.334
isn't it?

45:14.712 --> 45:16.964
I met an old friend not long ago.

45:17.506 --> 45:19.967
They told me
about a strange job they worked on,

45:20.467 --> 45:23.262
where they attached
hidden cameras to a light.

45:25.097 --> 45:27.182
I believe the lights were from France.

45:28.517 --> 45:31.854
They said they were rare.
That there are only a few in the country.

45:32.896 --> 45:34.481
A special order, that was it.

45:34.982 --> 45:37.317
They had to jump through hoops to buy it.

45:39.611 --> 45:40.446
I wonder…

45:43.574 --> 45:45.743
why anyone would put hidden cameras there.

45:54.418 --> 45:56.253
I'm just dying to find out.

46:24.907 --> 46:27.409
If I'm being completely honest,

46:27.993 --> 46:32.331
I didn't want to speak badly of someone
who's already dead,

46:32.831 --> 46:35.042
so I couldn't tell you everything
last time.

46:36.502 --> 46:37.711
The thing is,

46:38.420 --> 46:40.214
he didn't exactly seem normal.

46:41.840 --> 46:42.674
How so?

46:44.092 --> 46:45.636
Well,

46:46.553 --> 46:48.555
he had a knack for making enemies.

46:50.307 --> 46:52.017
I guess you could say he was unstable.

46:52.643 --> 46:55.938
Which individuals held ill will
towards Mr. Eom Tae-seong?

46:56.980 --> 46:58.690
I wouldn't know for sure,

46:58.774 --> 47:02.110
but I doubt anyone liked him
after interacting with him.

47:02.194 --> 47:04.530
Seo-yeon didn't seem to like him either.

47:04.613 --> 47:07.157
She said this in passing,
so I'm not sure if I heard her correctly,

47:08.951 --> 47:11.537
but I think she told me
that he tried to blackmail her.

47:14.873 --> 47:17.668
Then again, I don't know the whole story.

47:21.505 --> 47:22.589
"Blackmail"?

47:35.561 --> 47:37.145
Can we listen to just the sound effects?

47:37.229 --> 47:38.814
Sound effects, coming right up.

47:46.071 --> 47:49.533
I know a killer beef tripe hot pot place.
Want to have lunch together?

47:59.293 --> 48:00.961
Or I can just eat with Ms. In-ji.

48:17.311 --> 48:19.271
The stab wound is from way before he died,

48:19.354 --> 48:22.149
and judging by its size,
I'd say it was done with a fruit knife.

48:22.232 --> 48:23.233
It's pretty deep.

48:25.235 --> 48:29.156
- If Eom Tae-seong was stabbed this badly--
- He would have killed whoever stabbed him.

48:29.239 --> 48:31.074
Right, but we have nothing.

48:31.158 --> 48:33.160
No sign of a struggle or anything.

48:34.661 --> 48:36.914
- Do you think it was self-harm?
- What? This guy?

48:37.915 --> 48:39.583
And people don't self-harm just once.

48:40.083 --> 48:41.251
It's a habit.

48:52.596 --> 48:53.889
I thought you'd treat me.

48:55.182 --> 48:56.391
What do you have to say?

48:58.560 --> 48:59.686
That man's house

49:00.312 --> 49:03.649
has been vacant for five years,
but In-ji's been taking care of it.

49:04.942 --> 49:08.445
It hasn't changed at all since then.
She hasn't changed a thing.

49:10.781 --> 49:11.865
How do you know that?

49:16.328 --> 49:17.329
Picking a lock's easy.

49:20.582 --> 49:21.625
By the way…

49:23.919 --> 49:25.379
why do you think she picked you?

49:26.838 --> 49:30.425
In-ji's first and fourth husbands
were both suffering from diseases.

49:31.677 --> 49:32.511
Terminally ill.

49:33.011 --> 49:34.304
One of them was a gay guy

49:34.888 --> 49:37.140
who only got married
because his family insisted.

49:37.224 --> 49:38.433
And the other one…

49:40.727 --> 49:42.854
had no interest in doing it.

49:44.439 --> 49:46.650
Who knows if he didn't want to
or just couldn't?

49:47.234 --> 49:49.945
So why you?

49:54.449 --> 49:57.285
Did your wife divorce you
because you couldn't get it up?

49:59.997 --> 50:01.123
Come on,

50:02.290 --> 50:04.418
I'm just kidding.

50:10.173 --> 50:12.384
Anyway, the conclusion is…

50:18.098 --> 50:20.892
I think it's my destiny
to perish alongside Ms. In-ji.

50:22.811 --> 50:24.479
If I can't have her…

50:27.774 --> 50:29.276
maybe that wouldn't be so bad,

50:30.235 --> 50:31.361
don't you think?

50:35.407 --> 50:37.784
How long have you known Han Jeong-won?

50:38.410 --> 50:40.954
He must have been around 17 or so.

50:41.038 --> 50:42.330
After his mother's suicide,

50:43.081 --> 50:44.624
he started to rely on drugs.

50:46.585 --> 50:49.629
It was even a small story
on the news back then.

50:49.713 --> 50:53.467
"Underage son of corporate CEO
arrested for drug abuse."

50:53.550 --> 50:55.093
At the time, he was carrying

50:56.094 --> 50:58.513
a pill with a synthetic cannabinoid.

50:59.222 --> 51:01.558
You rarely see that kind of drug,
even today.

51:01.641 --> 51:03.518
It's time-consuming
and expensive to produce.

51:06.104 --> 51:07.397
It had an odd name,

51:07.481 --> 51:10.317
so between us,
we initially called it "the blue pill."

51:13.361 --> 51:14.780
Did he ever go back on it?

51:16.031 --> 51:19.951
I've always had my suspicions,
but I've always had no evidence.

51:21.995 --> 51:25.624
Did Han Jeong-won kill someone?

51:26.583 --> 51:27.501
Not yet.

51:27.584 --> 51:28.668
Please help yourself.

53:20.030 --> 53:21.740
The person you have called…

53:21.823 --> 53:23.783
NOH IN-JI

53:28.622 --> 53:29.456
Hello?

53:32.751 --> 53:34.044
Where are you now?

53:34.127 --> 53:35.003
You're home, right?

53:35.503 --> 53:37.589
I needed to leave
to take care of something.

53:38.173 --> 53:39.007
Where to?

53:39.674 --> 53:40.634
My old house.

53:41.635 --> 53:43.303
I'd appreciate it if you could come back.

53:45.180 --> 53:46.264
Is something wrong?

53:48.475 --> 53:50.477
Can you just come back home?

53:52.646 --> 53:54.022
Or I'll come to you.

53:54.105 --> 53:54.940
Where are you?

53:55.023 --> 53:56.233
This won't take long.

53:57.234 --> 53:58.151
I'll be back soon.

54:35.563 --> 54:36.398
What the…

54:42.904 --> 54:43.738
The heck?

54:47.534 --> 54:48.785
This is the right…

54:53.665 --> 54:55.375
What the fuck is going on?

54:59.337 --> 55:00.171
Damn it!

55:11.766 --> 55:12.684
Ms. In-ji?

58:56.157 --> 58:59.452
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
